WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.430
Do you really love Kyouka-sama herself?

00:03.430 --> 00:07.100
I'm incapable of loving someone.

00:03.430 --> 00:07.810
PLACEHOLDER

00:03.430 --> 00:07.810
Ouka-san, why are you thinking of something that makes you want to die just from pondering it?

00:07.100 --> 00:10.930
Even so, I do care about the family.

00:09.240 --> 00:12.530
PLACEHOLDER

00:09.240 --> 00:12.530
He might have had a family or a beloved person.

00:10.930 --> 00:14.330
Plus, I do like you.

00:12.530 --> 00:16.360
PLACEHOLDER

00:12.530 --> 00:16.360
It's all a trap set by God. The infinite Hell.

00:16.480 --> 00:18.600
PLACEHOLDER

00:16.480 --> 00:18.600
Does it not hurt you, Grim Reaper?

00:17.330 --> 00:19.870
Did you not see that?

00:19.320 --> 00:20.560
PLACEHOLDER

00:19.320 --> 00:20.560
To kill so much...

00:20.560 --> 00:24.870
PLACEHOLDER

00:20.560 --> 00:24.870
It's pointless for you to wish me to share your sense of vanity.

00:21.870 --> 00:24.870
I knew it. I was just worried for a second.

00:24.870 --> 00:27.880
PLACEHOLDER

00:24.870 --> 00:27.880
But I think you're fine that way, Ouka-san.

00:25.490 --> 00:27.880
Since I do get hung up sometimes.

00:27.880 --> 00:30.160
PLACEHOLDER

00:27.880 --> 00:29.900
If you were to become a Grim Reaper...

01:51.290 --> 01:54.670
My Darling Ouka - handsome, kind, and so charming.

01:54.670 --> 01:57.260
This is a story of Kyouka-sama who loves you so much, meow.

02:26.360 --> 02:27.330
Seven years old.

02:27.790 --> 02:31.100
She is a girl who's the same age as you, Ouka-kun.

02:32.000 --> 02:35.810
And like you, she lost her parents.

02:36.500 --> 02:42.190
A week ago, a paranormal phenomenon that's yet to be explained destroyed a village.

02:42.940 --> 02:46.410
What remained were countless mummified corpses.

02:46.990 --> 02:51.300
Among them, she is the only survivor and eyewitness.

02:52.190 --> 02:55.620
Your mission is to extract information from her.

02:56.080 --> 02:58.120
The mission is the only thing that interests you, right?

02:58.920 --> 03:01.150
You're really uncute.

03:15.160 --> 03:16.550
Hello.

03:19.400 --> 03:21.600
I simply bled when I started punching.

03:22.380 --> 03:23.970
Hey, are you strong?

03:24.420 --> 03:27.470
Will you be able to play with me without breaking easily?

03:38.260 --> 03:43.030
A seven year old girl just tried to kill a person without any hesitation.

03:43.630 --> 03:44.950
Could she be a prodigy?

03:44.950 --> 03:47.150
Grim Reaper II.

03:46.050 --> 03:50.530
Shunned by the world, but a monster humans desire.

03:59.190 --> 04:02.110
How dare he recover without my permission?!

04:02.110 --> 04:03.700
Ouka...

04:03.700 --> 04:07.900
He isn't understanding the role a husband is supposed to have!

04:07.900 --> 04:11.010
What's wrong? Kitty looks very upset.

04:11.010 --> 04:13.730
She says Father was missing when she woke up this morning.

04:13.730 --> 04:17.600
PLACEHOLDER

04:13.730 --> 04:17.600
Unforgivable! Unforgivable Ouka! You will pay for this!

04:14.100 --> 04:17.600
Oh, Ouka-san left early dressed up.

04:17.600 --> 04:18.110
What?

04:18.620 --> 04:19.630
Dressed up?

04:19.630 --> 04:21.890
That scarecrow is dressed up?

04:21.300 --> 04:22.580
Ch-Chika-chan.

04:22.850 --> 04:26.620
Dressed up was just the subjective opinion I formed.

04:26.620 --> 04:30.370
That scarecrow... That scarecrow dressed up and left?

04:30.370 --> 04:31.550
Suspicious!

04:31.550 --> 04:36.200
My sharp wild instinct is screaming, "Heave ho! Heave ho!" in my head!

04:36.200 --> 04:39.130
So Kitty's wild instinct must be related to festivals.

04:39.130 --> 04:42.220
Come to think of, Dad said he was going to an amusement park with a woman.

04:43.800 --> 04:45.480
H-Honored Sister!

04:45.480 --> 04:47.930
Why are you panicking so much, Teika-kun?

04:47.930 --> 04:50.180
We were supposed to keep where Father is a secret.

04:54.300 --> 04:55.580
So what's this?

04:56.340 --> 04:57.690
Is he cheating on me?!

04:59.400 --> 05:01.900
How brave for that Ouka to be doing this!

05:01.900 --> 05:04.310
I will praise you from the bottom of
my heart for the first time in your life!

05:04.310 --> 05:08.620
You're amazing to leave me here working while you go flirt with another woman!

05:04.820 --> 05:08.620
Mother, I'm watching TV, so can you quiet down?

05:26.450 --> 05:27.800
I'm sorry.

05:28.280 --> 05:29.850
How long did you wait?

05:30.580 --> 05:31.510
I've been waiting...

05:32.180 --> 05:33.770
...since my last life.

05:33.770 --> 05:35.340
A long time, then.

05:36.390 --> 05:38.480
Oh, just for ten minutes.

05:38.480 --> 05:41.930
Grim Reaper, I heard you went to hunt down ghouls.

05:41.930 --> 05:42.440
Yes.

05:42.960 --> 05:45.270
It's simultaneously the pursuit of my hobby and work.

05:45.270 --> 05:48.950
It is my life's pleasure to destroy a monster's face beautifully.

05:48.950 --> 05:52.430
That ghoul entertained me well.

05:52.430 --> 05:55.540
No matter how much I destroyed its face, it wouldn't die.

05:55.540 --> 05:57.370
And like that fragile skull was-

05:56.650 --> 05:58.370
I'm really glad to see you haven't changed at all.

06:00.990 --> 06:05.420
Rather than that, Ouka-san.
What did you mean by this being our last date?

06:05.420 --> 06:06.860
Well, not really a date, but...

06:06.860 --> 06:08.960
I did some research!

06:08.960 --> 06:14.770
I heard you're on a mission called
Operation Cozy Family to save the world.

06:14.770 --> 06:19.220
Then you do know I'm married and have a wife and children.

06:19.220 --> 06:20.500
Yes, I do.

06:20.500 --> 06:21.830
But what's the problem?

06:21.830 --> 06:23.750
"Problem?" Obviously...

06:24.110 --> 06:27.150
...coming to an amusement park with just the two of us is...

06:28.130 --> 06:31.320
You're slow with love and relationship issues as usual.

06:31.320 --> 06:33.840
The mission means nothing.

06:34.320 --> 06:40.670
What I want to hear is, Ouka-san,
who the goddess with a place in your heart is.

06:41.580 --> 06:43.770
Now, answer me.

06:43.770 --> 06:45.710
Don't disappoint me.

06:45.710 --> 06:48.720
I don't want to destroy your face, too.

06:55.010 --> 06:57.600
Keep your hands off the god's husband, you poisonous wench!

06:57.600 --> 06:58.580
Kyouka!

06:58.580 --> 07:02.600
Ouka-san, could that crazy cat-eared child be your wife?

07:03.220 --> 07:06.920
If I'd known he was meeting a masked specter like you, then there wouldn't have been a need to worry.

07:06.920 --> 07:08.240
But let me say it to be sure!

07:08.240 --> 07:12.420
You cat burglar who tries to butt in between the happy couple and destroy the house!

07:12.420 --> 07:13.320
Get lost already!

07:14.560 --> 07:16.840
I wonder who the cat burglar is.

07:16.840 --> 07:20.710
I've been together with Ouka-san for twenty years.

07:20.710 --> 07:25.420
I have a bond with him incomparable to yours.

07:26.530 --> 07:28.320
I live with him.

07:28.320 --> 07:29.870
You can't beat the bond of a family, now can you?

07:29.870 --> 07:32.260
If it's just living together, even a dog can do it.

07:32.260 --> 07:32.840
Grim Reaper!

07:32.840 --> 07:35.320
You've got a good mouth, you bitch!

07:35.320 --> 07:37.330
If the world allowed it, you'd be charged for lèse majesté and sentenced to beheading.

07:37.330 --> 07:41.110
What world are you talking about?
Perhaps the world of crickets or weeds?

07:41.110 --> 07:42.790
What did you say?

07:41.980 --> 07:43.690
Stop this, both of you!

07:44.290 --> 07:47.100
I'm sorry, but could you go home for today, Kyouka?

07:47.100 --> 07:49.930
Your presence only makes matters more complicated.

07:49.930 --> 07:52.850
I want to have a conversation alone with Grim Reaper.

07:52.850 --> 07:56.330
Alone... Alone... Alone...

07:55.080 --> 07:56.330
Hold me tighter.

07:56.330 --> 07:57.450
Alone...

07:58.020 --> 07:59.480
I didn't mean it like that.

07:59.480 --> 08:02.250
So you want to flirt with the other woman that much?

08:01.560 --> 08:02.250
No, I mean-

08:02.250 --> 08:03.870
Let's talk just the two of us, shall we?

08:06.380 --> 08:08.090
G-Grim Reaper, what are you doing?

08:08.090 --> 08:09.870
Then do as you please.

08:09.870 --> 08:11.490
I'm saying it's not like that.

08:11.490 --> 08:13.220
Your name was Grim Reaper, right?

08:13.220 --> 08:13.970
That's me.

08:13.220 --> 08:13.970
Kyouka!

08:14.760 --> 08:15.840
You!

08:15.840 --> 08:16.760
Kyouka?

08:16.760 --> 08:21.480
You just made the being in the world whom you most wish not to become your enemy... into your enemy!

08:25.860 --> 08:29.480
Remember this! I will bring misery to both of you!

08:29.480 --> 08:32.170
She stepped down more easily than I'd thought.

08:32.170 --> 08:34.280
I can't even imagine what she'll do to me when I go home.

08:34.280 --> 08:36.140
You're having a scary married life like that?

08:36.140 --> 08:39.810
I shall destroy her face after all.

08:38.740 --> 08:40.450
I beg you, please stop.

08:45.860 --> 08:50.630
Remember this! I will bring misery to both of you!

08:49.420 --> 08:51.960
Hey, Onee-chan went home?

08:51.960 --> 08:53.660
Odessa Ei is puzzled?

08:53.660 --> 08:57.770
I thought Onee-chan would follow if I drew out this Ouka person.

08:58.150 --> 08:58.550
Hey.

09:00.560 --> 09:08.610
Ouka-san, if you say you don't want to go on dates with me anymore, then that makes this our last memory in the making.

09:09.480 --> 09:12.630
But of course, I don't have any intention of making this the last.

09:12.630 --> 09:15.310
If we spend a day together,
I'm sure your mind will change, too.

09:15.310 --> 09:16.100
Grim Reaper...

09:16.100 --> 09:18.620
Anyway, we have to have lots of fun today.

09:18.620 --> 09:20.760
Wait, Grim Reaper!

09:20.760 --> 09:26.540
What? That's not the amusement park Odessa Ei set traps in.

09:26.540 --> 09:28.390
Things aren't turning out as I want.

09:28.390 --> 09:30.970
Why won't you fall into misery like I want you to?

09:36.550 --> 09:38.140
Desu~

09:38.550 --> 09:39.930
Desu~

09:40.550 --> 09:42.560
Desu~

09:43.560 --> 09:45.770
I'll get something cold.

09:45.770 --> 09:47.380
Wait, I'll-

09:47.380 --> 09:49.940
You rest right here.

09:57.810 --> 09:59.130
Is it good?

10:03.130 --> 10:03.760
Here.

10:04.330 --> 10:06.550
Chocolate mint, right?

10:07.210 --> 10:08.190
Thank you.

10:08.190 --> 10:12.750
I've known you for a long time, so I know all your favorites.

10:15.310 --> 10:21.260
Every day is full of anxiety since I question what I'm doing.

10:22.170 --> 10:24.220
But that's fun at the same time.

10:24.720 --> 10:30.650
While I know it's a mission, when I think,
"What if this family breaks apart?" it really hurts me.

10:31.400 --> 10:33.740
This is the first time I've ever felt like this.

10:35.400 --> 10:39.350
It's not very like you to express your feelings, Ouka-san.

10:39.350 --> 10:40.820
You're scaring me.

10:40.820 --> 10:45.740
You're right. In the past, I might have changed the topic.

10:46.980 --> 10:48.000
Grim Reaper.

10:48.000 --> 10:48.690
Yes?

10:49.320 --> 10:53.540
Initially, I started this convincing myself that it's a mission.

10:57.250 --> 11:01.020
Even though I thought
Operation Cozy Family sounded dumb,

11:01.540 --> 11:05.930
I told myself that I'd play the best husband role since it's a mission.

11:06.260 --> 11:09.060
That's very like you, the diligent Ouka-san.

11:09.060 --> 11:11.270
But this isn't working at all.

11:13.380 --> 11:15.740
We're alike, remember?

11:15.740 --> 11:19.030
We can't trust or believe in others.

11:25.270 --> 11:28.080
So we can't possibly love people.

11:28.080 --> 11:29.310
You're imagining things!

11:29.310 --> 11:32.890
It's all your imagination!
You're wishing that it would come true.

11:32.890 --> 11:33.710
Wish?

11:35.220 --> 11:37.170
You're such a persistent woman, aren't you?

11:39.860 --> 11:43.050
Being with an ugly woman like you makes me wanna puke.

11:44.100 --> 11:45.220
That wasn't me!

11:45.220 --> 11:46.130
Kyouka?

11:46.130 --> 11:47.310
Do you hate me?

11:47.310 --> 11:48.670
N-No!

11:50.260 --> 11:53.380
A masked woman like me makes you sick, is that right?

11:53.730 --> 11:56.310
I've hated a monster like you for years.

11:58.140 --> 12:00.500
I don't even want to see your face, so can I go home now?

12:00.850 --> 12:03.280
Ouka-san... Is that your answer?

12:03.280 --> 12:04.570
I'm saying it isn't!

12:04.570 --> 12:06.910
I will destroy your face!

12:36.380 --> 12:39.660
Could you possibly be Teika?

12:39.960 --> 12:44.110
I am unrelated to your son, Teika.

12:44.110 --> 12:45.780
You just admitted it yourself.

12:46.500 --> 12:48.150
Why are you here, Teika?

12:48.150 --> 12:49.680
Did Kyouka send you?

12:49.680 --> 12:51.540
What is she planning?

12:51.540 --> 12:53.290
You're not a foolish person, Father.

12:53.870 --> 12:56.670
So I trust that you will not betray Mother.

12:56.670 --> 12:59.540
Then why are you helping Kyouka?

13:00.030 --> 13:03.920
I simply want to prove your innocence!

13:03.920 --> 13:05.550
Our bond!

13:09.850 --> 13:11.810
Welcome.

13:12.810 --> 13:14.310
Welcome.

13:16.780 --> 13:17.960
You all...

13:22.820 --> 13:25.420
You detest ugly faces?

13:25.420 --> 13:27.350
You detest monsters?

13:30.640 --> 13:32.290
Grim Reaper II!

13:32.290 --> 13:35.860
Shiruku, don't you wish to become strong?

13:36.320 --> 13:41.140
Do you wish to become a being which can destroy monsters with brute strength alone?

13:42.360 --> 13:49.180
You cannot forgive yourself for not being able to do anything but watch your parents and friends die, right?

13:49.550 --> 13:51.750
Then become a Grim Reaper.

13:51.750 --> 13:54.310
You have the right and talent to do so.

14:04.860 --> 14:08.250
I swore to forsake being human since that day.

14:08.250 --> 14:12.600
The title Grim Reaper is only given to those who have killed a thousand monsters.

14:14.120 --> 14:17.550
This scorched face I received in battle is my pride as a Grim Reaper.

14:17.550 --> 14:22.380
Yet my heart falls to pieces just from one person rejecting me.

14:23.130 --> 14:24.880
I'm tired of waiting.

14:24.880 --> 14:25.920
You!

14:25.920 --> 14:31.970
It's funny to watch you play the tragic heroine role with that face, but I want to end things soon, too.

14:34.310 --> 14:39.430
You're brave to fight me unarmed, but you seem to lack brains.

14:39.430 --> 14:41.640
I can beat you with my eyes closed!

14:45.780 --> 14:46.990
Not bad.

14:46.990 --> 14:48.290
Since I'm a god, after all.

14:48.290 --> 14:50.950
I'm referred to as a god of death, too.

14:54.410 --> 14:56.520
I guess the match is settled.

15:00.860 --> 15:02.920
You can't, Grim Reaper.

15:02.920 --> 15:05.500
Odessa Ei will be the one to beat Onee-chan.

15:06.820 --> 15:08.190
This won't do.

15:08.190 --> 15:10.090
I need to make you suffer more.

15:11.050 --> 15:15.780
Onee-chan's finally come back,
so do move as I wish, okay, Grim Reaper?

15:15.780 --> 15:16.990
It's this voice again.

15:16.990 --> 15:18.390
Who is it?

15:20.890 --> 15:23.900
Sir, is this your first time at a place like this?

15:24.470 --> 15:26.330
What is this about?

15:26.330 --> 15:28.870
Don't be looking so scary.

15:28.870 --> 15:31.650
It's important to relax once in a while.

15:31.650 --> 15:32.780
H-Here's your drink!

15:33.340 --> 15:35.320
Alcohol is only allowed after you're of age!

15:35.320 --> 15:36.170
Yuuka?

15:36.170 --> 15:37.710
What are you talking about?

15:37.710 --> 15:40.410
I'm simply staff at this shop.

15:40.810 --> 15:45.090
Could you tell Daddy what's going on, Yuuka?

15:45.090 --> 15:46.700
I am not Yuuka!

15:46.700 --> 15:47.920
I'm some other person!

15:47.920 --> 15:50.330
Anyways, I'll listen to the story later.

15:50.330 --> 15:51.920
I'm a little busy, so may I go?

15:51.920 --> 15:54.140
Ah, you're so cold.

15:54.140 --> 15:56.650
If you're leaving, you'll owe us ¥4,000,000.

15:56.650 --> 15:57.430
¥4,000,000?!

15:57.430 --> 16:01.600
In shops like this, body touches with
a girl get added to the check, too.

16:01.600 --> 16:03.590
Hey, you're getting carried away!

16:04.590 --> 16:07.550
But this is who I really am!

16:07.550 --> 16:09.860
Right now, Ginka-chan's like a fish rejuvenated in water.

16:09.860 --> 16:11.360
So you are Ginka.

16:11.970 --> 16:16.700
Sir, you have to pay for the drink the moment it's poured into your glass.

16:16.700 --> 16:21.540
B-But if you stay here for another hour,
it'll only cost you ¥1,000.

16:21.540 --> 16:25.160
I see. You want to lock me up in this shop.

16:25.160 --> 16:25.880
You're not getting away!

16:25.880 --> 16:28.340
We even have guards here.

16:31.170 --> 16:32.630
Ouka-san.

16:32.630 --> 16:33.470
Grim Reaper.

16:34.630 --> 16:39.920
I'm glad. You were kidnapped by a stuffed doll, so I was worrying in what kind of bizarre situation you could be in.

16:39.920 --> 16:41.100
I'm sorry-

16:42.490 --> 16:45.080
I'm busy fooling around with these girls!

16:45.080 --> 16:46.360
You're so persistent!

16:46.360 --> 16:50.240
Oh, Father. So you're finally in the mood.

16:51.060 --> 16:54.110
Masked women like me are disgusting, right?

16:54.110 --> 16:55.490
I wonder what I was thinking.

16:56.790 --> 16:57.740
I get it now.

16:57.740 --> 16:59.330
Father.

17:02.790 --> 17:05.160
Kyouka. I'll wait five seconds.

17:05.160 --> 17:07.170
Stop this mess within that time.

17:14.080 --> 17:17.110
I haven't been this seriously mad in a while.

17:17.720 --> 17:23.300
I've experienced many annoyances since meeting you,
but I'm angrier at this than any other incident.

17:23.300 --> 17:25.140
I can feel my heart freezing away.

17:26.640 --> 17:30.260
If you don't put an end to this, I'll scorn you.

17:30.260 --> 17:32.140
I'll hate you.

17:32.140 --> 17:33.860
I'll die hating you.

17:41.270 --> 17:43.580
Die if you want to.

17:43.580 --> 17:45.030
Mother...

17:45.030 --> 17:46.330
That's what I'd like to say.

17:46.330 --> 17:50.040
But that will likely make my mornings gloomy, so I won't.

17:54.760 --> 17:56.300
Mother...

18:00.330 --> 18:03.750
Ow ow ow ow!

18:00.340 --> 18:01.970
You big moron!

18:03.750 --> 18:06.350
Does it hurt? Yes, I'm sure it does.

18:04.350 --> 18:09.020
PLACEHOLDER

18:04.350 --> 18:09.020
I never imagined I'd get yelled at in such a unique manner.

18:08.570 --> 18:10.440
I'm sorry, Grim Reaper.

18:09.020 --> 18:12.530
PLACEHOLDER

18:09.020 --> 18:12.530
It's stretching! It's stretching!

18:10.830 --> 18:13.370
Everything was set up by her.

18:12.530 --> 18:15.370
PLACEHOLDER

18:12.530 --> 18:15.260
You're keeping me in the air! You're keeping me in the air!

18:13.730 --> 18:15.260
You all go back home.

18:15.260 --> 18:19.280
I'm not planning to abandon the Midarezaki family or disbanding it at all.

18:15.260 --> 18:19.030
PLACEHOLDER
PLACEHOLDER

18:15.260 --> 18:19.030
It'll tear! It'll tear! It'll tear!

18:26.830 --> 18:31.880
Even if I tried to get time alone with him, you'd keep on bothering us, right?

18:31.880 --> 18:37.500
I can't stand my possessions being owned by someone else for a day. Not even for a second!

18:38.530 --> 18:42.180
Then it's much better for the three of us to be together in the first place.

18:43.230 --> 18:43.970
What?

18:44.410 --> 18:46.800
What are you planning, Grim Reaper?

18:46.800 --> 18:50.000
I'm compromising with you this much,
yet you still suspect me?

18:50.000 --> 18:53.800
Well, I guess it'll be a good opportunity for me to judge you.

18:53.800 --> 18:55.100
"Judge" you say?

18:55.100 --> 18:57.900
A grim reaper like you will render judgment upon a god-

18:57.900 --> 19:00.820
If you utter more selfishness, I really will have you go home.

19:00.820 --> 19:05.580
PLACEHOLDER
PLACEHOLDER

19:00.820 --> 19:05.580
Damn you, don't say I'm selfish! I'm a god!

19:01.820 --> 19:07.870
Kyouka-san, if at the end of the day, I judge you to be insignificant, I will kill you then.

19:05.580 --> 19:07.870
PLACEHOLDER
PLACEHOLDER

19:05.580 --> 19:07.870
My hands won't reach!

19:15.830 --> 19:17.380
This place looks dead.

19:17.760 --> 19:19.670
I prefer the last one.

19:20.010 --> 19:23.260
We can't possibly go back after what we've done there.

19:24.330 --> 19:25.260
Three adults please.

19:26.650 --> 19:28.520
Odessa Ei is lucky?

19:28.520 --> 19:30.060
It's as I wished?

19:30.060 --> 19:33.480
You're finally falling into the trap I set, Onee-chan.

19:43.140 --> 19:45.060
PLACEHOLDER

19:43.140 --> 19:45.060
Welcome to Slave War Amusement Park.

19:45.060 --> 19:47.410
PLACEHOLDER

19:45.060 --> 19:47.410
Welcome. Welcome. Welcome.

19:46.390 --> 19:48.970
This is the guide robot that takes you around the park,

19:47.410 --> 19:49.050
PLACEHOLDER

19:47.410 --> 19:49.050
Hello. Hello.

19:48.970 --> 19:51.370
Baron Golden Swan.

19:49.050 --> 19:51.370
PLACEHOLDER

19:49.050 --> 19:51.370
Welcome. Enjoy.

19:51.370 --> 19:54.110
PLACEHOLDER

19:51.370 --> 19:54.110
Hello. Hello. Hello.

19:51.890 --> 19:53.770
That's a wastefully majestic name.

19:54.110 --> 19:58.630
Okay, I shall name you Trash the Third.

19:54.110 --> 19:57.880
PLACEHOLDER

19:54.110 --> 19:57.880
Welcome. Welcome. Welcome. Welcome.

19:58.630 --> 20:03.340
What a devil. You're such a devil, you may be executed later.

19:58.630 --> 20:03.340
PLACEHOLDER
PLACEHOLDER

19:58.630 --> 20:03.340
Dear customer! Please keep your hands off me!

19:59.420 --> 20:03.340
T-R-A-S-H.

20:05.130 --> 20:10.610
This amusement park has war as its theme, as the name implies.

20:10.610 --> 20:11.900
Flying bullets.

20:11.900 --> 20:13.030
The cries of your comrades.

20:13.030 --> 20:14.280
A drama of life and death.

20:15.270 --> 20:20.240
We are entering your first attraction,
a battle reenaction, War of Nagashino.

20:20.600 --> 20:22.070
Everyone, charge!

20:22.070 --> 20:23.210
Are we charging?

20:23.210 --> 20:24.410
We are charging.

20:24.410 --> 20:27.310
It's a reenactment of Takeda's cavalry,
renowned as the strongest in the Sengoku era,

20:27.310 --> 20:30.620
losing to Oda Nobunaga's gun troops.

20:31.590 --> 20:32.250
Get out!

20:33.790 --> 20:36.300
What is this? Is this part of the attraction?

20:36.300 --> 20:38.340
This can't possibly be part of the attraction!

20:39.960 --> 20:42.430
They're probably modern rifles.

20:42.430 --> 20:45.680
Take a headshot, and everything above your head will blow.

20:45.680 --> 20:50.310
What kind of group has a grudge
against you, you bad luck magnet?

20:50.310 --> 20:53.200
If anyone here is responsible
for a grudge, it'd be you, Grim Reaper!

20:53.200 --> 20:55.170
Don't fight in a situation like this!

20:55.170 --> 20:58.380
First we have to get out of this confined area.

20:58.380 --> 21:00.020
It's boring, but it's the correct idea.

21:02.110 --> 21:06.450
Grim Reaper, please destroy the wall two meters ahead with a grenade.

21:06.860 --> 21:07.490
Yes.

21:10.610 --> 21:11.450
Kyouka!

21:17.120 --> 21:20.160
Grim Reaper, are you trying to kill Kyouka?

21:20.160 --> 21:23.630
You wouldn't die from a grenade, would you, Onee-chan?

21:26.340 --> 21:27.260
Onee-chan?

21:27.260 --> 21:29.010
Grim Reaper, what's with those ears?

21:29.010 --> 21:30.580
We meet at last.

21:30.580 --> 21:32.520
Odessa Ei is really happy?

21:33.470 --> 21:34.770
Who the hell are you?!

21:35.360 --> 21:38.130
It's a waste to end this in an instant.

21:38.130 --> 21:41.410
I'll kill you in the most painful way.

21:41.410 --> 21:44.010
Why do you call me sister?

21:44.010 --> 21:47.280
Wow, this is interesting. You don't remember anything, eh?

21:47.280 --> 21:48.770
Onee-chan!

21:48.770 --> 21:49.520
Kyouka!

21:50.660 --> 21:54.540
Do you know exactly who I am?

21:55.020 --> 21:57.430
Sure, I'll tell you who you are.

22:00.580 --> 22:03.630
After that, I'll shred you to pieces.

23:41.100 --> 23:45.020
Mom! Mom! Amusement parks are really scary places, aren't they?

23:45.020 --> 23:46.110
By the way...

23:47.530 --> 23:49.280
I haven't had much screen time, have I?

23:50.150 --> 23:52.990
Next time: God and Grim Reaper's Party.
